[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-WHITEBOARD-VIEW-LEGEND
TITLE: How to read the colours
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: legend
PLACE: card
STATEMENT: >>>
Colour is only ever a legend word, and the word is always written out beside it. The first four words say how settled a ruling or a program is; the last three belong to the rules tab and say who enforces a rule today.

- ACCEPTED: green: in force
- OPEN: blue: a question
- SETTLED: teal: designed, not built
- BUILT: green: code landed
- STRICTDOC: slate: strictdoc already refuses it
- SCRIPT: amber: a rule in a script, indexed here
- UNBUILT: red: nobody enforces it
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
NAR-TERM-STRICTDOC:0000000
<<<
